{"type": "standard", "title": "Isorhythm", "displaytitle": "<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Isorhythm</span></span>", "namespace": {"id": 0, "text": ""}, "wikibase_item": "Q250765", "titles": {"canonical": "Isorhythm", "normalized": "Isorhythm", "display": "<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Isorhythm</span></span>"}, "pageid": 593718, "thumbnail": {"source": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/TenMachautKyrie.jpg/330px-TenMachautKyrie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail", "width": 330, "height": 157}, "originalimage": {"source": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bf/TenMachautKyrie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled", "width": 1074, "height": 511}, "lang": "en", "dir": "ltr", "revision": "1322163626", "tid": "e8d9927d-c181-11f0-8901-f1f604989d89", "timestamp": "2025-11-14T17:46:55Z", "description": "Musical technique using a repeating pattern", "description_source": "local", "content_urls": {"desktop": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isorhythm", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isorhythm?action=history", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isorhythm?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Isorhythm"}, "mobile": {"page": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isorhythm", "revisions": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Isorhythm", "edit": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isorhythm?action=edit", "talk": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Isorhythm"}}, "extract": "Isorhythm is a musical technique using a repeating rhythmic pattern, called a talea, in at least one voice part throughout a composition. Taleae are typically applied to one or more melodic patterns of pitches or colores, which may be of the same or a different length from the talea.", "extract_html": "<p><b>Isorhythm</b> is a musical technique using a repeating rhythmic pattern, called a <i>talea</i>, in at least one voice part throughout a composition. <i>Taleae</i> are typically applied to one or more melodic patterns of pitches or <i>colores</i>, which may be of the same or a different length from the <i>talea</i>.</p>"}